on":{"commit_sha":"2168411e8b4f154079d438179149a4849d7bb0ba","position":"1788409442352701001-37540706-459c-44a5-af5b-859862e42c95"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a9fa5d69464686e65266b3d1945b9533f111207a4f2194ad4cb406c37e503a64","event_uuid":"ed16fb2a-12db-469e-aa0d-797995ddc127","position":{"commit_sha":"c2c99ab2c0defa10e4de98aba0480657332ea11f","position":"1788409449117536001-ed16fb2a-12db-469e-aa0d-797995ddc127"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Handoff state. Plan CERTIFIED and ticket claimed. A subagent is implementing it in its OWN isolated worktree, branched from origin/main so it lands as an INDEPENDENT change rather than stacking on the six-change stack (which is currently Verified -1).\n\nThe plan was corrected once before certifying, and the correction matters: a module-scope `from rebar.config import LAYER_ORDER` would CYCLE, because config.py:99-101 imports FROM rebar._operation_config, which is the leaf. The shipped approach is a functools.cache accessor with a deferred import, following the precedent already in that module at :199-200.","timestamp":1788398802625402001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Two process notes from implementation.\n\n1. This ticket was worked while still `open`. My subagent brief asserted it was already claimed; it was not, and I told the agent not to run tracker writes, so nothing corrected it. Claimed now, retroactively — recording it rather than quietly fixing it, because 'claim before you work' is exactly the discipline that keeps the board honest about who holds what.\n\n2. AC1b as originally written was UNSATISFIABLE and has been corrected. It asked for `'rebar.config' not in sys.modules` after importing `rebar._operation_config`, but `rebar/__init__.py:27` does `from rebar import config`, so that is true on unmodified main as well — verified by running it. The criterion would have been red before and after, pinning the package __init__ rather than this change. It now asserts cache_info() misses at import versus after first call, plus AST assertions that no module-scope import names rebar.config and that the import lives inside the accessor body. A mutation hoisting the import to module scope turns those RED with the circular-import traceback.\n\nImplemented and pushed as Gerrit change 2547 from an isolated worktree, branched from origin/main so it does NOT stack on the six-change stack that is currently Verified -1.","timestamp":1788399318626375001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788317688277335001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"5c6cfba8-51a9-4a74-9b03-ff2ab375fae4","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"f9b9-83ad-931c-4833"},{"link_uuid":"4bb997a5-b99b-4a3c-8984-4e368ad375ad","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"59dd-e6ac-e2b6-4285"}],"description":"Mirror inventory finding F9 (`reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md`), LOW.\n\n## Problem\n\n- `src/rebar/config.py:326` `LAYER_ORDER = (\"default\", \"user\", \"project\", \"env\", \"cli\")` — canonical\n- `src/rebar/_operation_config.py:51` `_SOURCE_KINDS` — the same 5, hand-copied\n\n`_operation_config.py:128` validates a provenance label against the copy, and `config.py:337`\ndocuments that domain as \"``label`` ∈ :data:`LAYER_ORDER`\" — so the copy is asserting membership of\nthe canonical tuple while restating it.\n\n## Approach — a DEFERRED, cached derivation (a module-scope import would cycle)\n\nThe obvious fix — `_SOURCE_KINDS = frozenset(config.LAYER_ORDER)` at module scope — does NOT\nwork, and the reason is the substance of this ticket. The dependency runs the OTHER way:\n`config.py:99-101` imports `ENVELOPE_VERSION`, `OperationSnapshot` and `active_snapshot` FROM\n`rebar._operation_config`. `_operation_config` is the LEAF (its imports are stdlib only), so a\nmodule-scope `from rebar.config import LAYER_ORDER` would close the loop\nconfig -> _operation_config -> config at import time.\n\nSo derive it behind a cached accessor with a deferred import:\n\n    @functools.cache\n    def _source_kinds() -> frozenset[str]:\n        from rebar.config import LAYER_ORDER\n        return frozenset(LAYER_ORDER)\n\n`functools` is already imported here, and the deferred-import pattern is ALREADY established in\nthis module for exactly this cycle — `:199-200` does `from rebar import config as _config` inside\na function. There is one consumer (`:128`), so the constant-to-accessor change is contained.\n\nORDER is the tuple's only additional fact, and that consumer uses it purely as a membership test\n(`label not in ...`), so a frozenset loses nothing. That is worth stating rather than assuming: a\nset derivation would be wrong if any consumer depended on precedence, and none does — the only\nother reader of `LAYER_ORDER`, `_commands/show_config.py:52`, takes `list(...)` from config\ndirectly and is untouched.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] AC1: the source-kind vocabulary is derived from `config.LAYER_ORDER`, not re-listed.\n      Verified by a test asserting equality with `frozenset(config.LAYER_ORDER)` and the literal\n      being gone.\n- [x] AC1b: the derivation is DEFERRED — it does not run at import time. Verified in a clean\n      interpreter by asserting `_source_kinds.cache_info().misses == 0` immediately after\n      importing the module, then `1` after the first call and still `1` after the second, plus\n      two AST assertions: no module-scope import names `rebar.config`, and `rebar.config` IS\n      imported inside `_source_kinds`'s body.\n\n      **Corrected during implementation.** This criterion originally asked for\n      `'rebar.config' not in sys.modules` after importing `rebar._operation_config`. That\n      assertion is unsatisfiable and pins the wrong thing: `rebar/__init__.py:27` does\n      `from rebar import config`, and `_operation_config`'s own module-scope\n      `from rebar._config_coercion import ConfigError` forces the package init, so\n      `rebar.config` is in `sys.modules` on unmodified `main` too — verified by running it. It\n      would have been red before and after the change. The oracles above pin the property the\n      ticket actually cares about, and a mutation that hoists the import to module scope turns\n      them RED with the circular-import traceback.\n- [x] AC2: a layer added to `LAYER_ORDER` is accepted as a provenance label with no second edit.\n      Verified by a test that extends the compared tuple and asserts the derived set follows.\n- [x] AC3: no consumer of `_SOURCE_KINDS` relies on ordering, so the tuple -> frozenset conversion\n      is safe. Verified by a test asserting every use site treats it as a membership set.\n- [x] AC4: an unknown provenance label is still rejected. Verified by an explicit rejection test.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit -k \"operation_config or config_layer or provenance\" -q` — AC1-AC4.\n- `make lint && make typecheck`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_operation_config.py","reason":"derive _SOURCE_KINDS from config.LAYER_ORDER"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_operation_config_source_kinds.py","reason":"the oracle"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","f79d-0d71-0fd7-439f"],["relates_to","59dd-e6ac-e2b6-4285"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"f79d-0d71-0fd7-439f","parent_status_uuid":"37540706-459c-44a5-af5b-859862e42c95","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"70f5-2253-1671-474d","ticket_type":"task","title":"Derive _operation_config._SOURCE_KINDS from config.LAYER_ORDER (mirror F9)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c14b1e50-4697-4255-9cb8-1af7d5f04a39","a2e981d7-0822-4464-be24-6421c0833bfb","05f47f36-c137-4580-b697-fad01d00babc","fc40f66e-cdb8-44ae-81d1-4a9c2b254b2e","f492be91-e4d0-4722-8a0c-5199aed9d2be","e072db44-1ca9-4fa5-9730-b303f7457797","50cefc85-0476-4940-bfab-2d2982894922","db8e9e71-bb5f-4377-8d48-d47b5b740d8a","bfe3e013-2661-41de-9367-7f405c9f1639","4bb997a5-b99b-4a3c-8984-4e368ad375ad","e0812aa4-0c43-4ef4-94fa-760f79aa31a3","701f037d-fcf9-4db6-8777-be909cad0032","37540706-459c-44a5-af5b-859862e42c95","ed16fb2a-12db-469e-aa0d-797995ddc127"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788411701200591001,"uuid":"06f0ad6e-0d52-472a-bcf5-d7217b7e02b5"}